<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Estácio de Sá</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1520">1520</a>–1567</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Estácio de Sá was a Portuguese soldier, nephew of the governor-general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mem-de-sa">Mem de Sá</a>, who founded the city of São Sebastião do <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> on 1 March 1565 at the foot of Sugarloaf Mountain. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temimino">Temiminó</a> allies he fought to drive the French and their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tupinamba">Tupinambá</a> allies from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanabara-bay">Guanabara Bay</a>, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> Antarctique. He died of an arrow wound received in the decisive battle of 1567.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/estacio-de-sa.jpg" alt="Estácio de Sá" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Junius · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Funda%C3%A7%C3%A3o_do_Rio_de_Janeiro.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
